+## Submission and Idempotency
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit edit with valid field types and a valid plot reference with a new idempotency key, the system SHALL store the submission with its visit ID, base revision ID, submitted values, author ID, and server receipt time, and return the generated submission ID and acceptance timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original submission ID and acceptance timestamp without creating another submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
-- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+
+## Current State Retrieval
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a caller retrieves a visit with a single accepted revision, the system SHALL return that revision's data, revision ID, and no resolution status indicator.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a caller retrieves a visit that has been resolved by a coordinator selection, the system SHALL return the selected revision's data, revision ID, and resolution status "resolved".
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a caller retrieves a visit with competing revisions (multiple submissions from the same base revision), the system SHALL return all competing submission payloads with their submission IDs, authors, and resolution status "unresolved" instead of a single current revision.
+
+## Competing Revisions
+
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When two or more submissions are accepted against the same base revision ID, the system SHALL store all submissions as a competing set and not automatically combine their fields.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When retrieving unresolved competing revisions, the system SHALL return all competing submission payloads with their submission IDs and authors so a coordinator can compare them.
+
+## Resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-030**: When a coordinator resolves competing revisions by selecting one submission ID as authoritative, the system SHALL store the resolution with the coordinator ID, selected submission ID, and resolution timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-031**: After a coordinator resolution, calls to retrieve that visit SHALL return the selected submission as current and resolution status as "resolved".
+- [ ] **REC-032**: When a coordinator resolves a visit, the system SHALL retain all original submissions and the resolution record for audit.
+
+## Data Preservation
+
+- [ ] **REC-040**: The system SHALL never silently discard a submitted edit, whether or not a coordinator selects it as authoritative.
